From: Galdrun <galdrun@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mwifiex: pcie: drain recovery work before clearing adapter

Unbinding can time out a firmware command and queue dump/reset work. The
worker dereferences card->adapter, but unregister_dev clears it before
cleanup_pcie eventually drains that worker. Drain it while the adapter is
still valid, retaining the existing reset-path exception to avoid waiting
on the worker from its own PCI reset callback.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/pcie.c
@@ -3202,6 +3202,10 @@ static void mwifiex_unregister_dev(struct mwifiex_adapter *adapter)
 		if (card->msi_enable)
 			pci_disable_msi(pdev);
 	}
+	/* Drain dump/reset work before invalidating its adapter pointer. */
+	if (!card->pci_reset_ongoing)
+		cancel_work_sync(&card->work);
+
 	card->adapter = NULL;
 }
 
